Z||000000||Formula 18||07-03-2000||12:41 AM||||My question is: <BR>Is there any way that I can lower the Idle and or Trick the computer into thinking the EGR is working ok. See story for more info. <P><BR>My story is:<BR>OK here's the deal my Idle was way way low the other night when I took my 88 Formula out so today I climbed under the car to see what was up. After look at a couple of things I noticed that the EGR valve was just hanging by the stem. Upon closer inspection I noticed that the Selonoid Part was toally broken off for the manifold (the three little metal clips the held it on were all broken). So after breaking one of the bolts that holds it and taking the other off I tried to acr weld it back together (not a good idea b/c once i brushed of the rust there was not much left to weld). I made some "gaskets" W/o any holes out of a thin sheet meatle so that any holes in the manifolds were pluged. I was so proud I thought fixed the problemand didn't even have to buy any new parts, fired up my baby and now it idles at 1500. So any ideas on how to make it idle at like a Grand w/o an EGR? <P><BR>BTW-- for you Gov't watch dog's I know it is illegal but eill put everything back in working order ASA I can get the parts.||||reg||1
Z||000001||shain||07-03-2000||03:36 AM||||go out tomorrow and get a new valve you cheap ass!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||07-03-2000||10:16 AM||||If you block off the EGR and the idle is still high you may have a vacuum leak under the plenum or one of the vacuum lines for the solinoid. If the EGR was hanging one of the hard plastic vacuum lines could have cracked or split. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula 18||07-03-2000||01:41 PM||||Shain-<BR>Thanks for the help. BTW if you read my post I didn't say that I didn't have the money but we have A parts store and you can't just walk in a say, "Hi, I need a EGR assembly for a 88 Formula" and they throw it on the table. <P>Orief- <BR>Where do I look for the leak? You can push the EGR valve in by hand and it will drop the idle back to aout 900, so i don't think it is leaking. It just broken for that cast iron piece that holds it to the manifold. <P>Anyone else got any idea on how to disable this puppy for a bit Just till the past come in??? ||||reg||1
